Scope of the MIT licence
------------------------
The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the contents of this repository only: the
two definition files under src/def/, the manifest and description, the build
and image scripts, and the documentation. All of it is original work.

No game content is included
---------------------------
This repository contains no files from Euro Truck Simulator 2. No models, no
textures, no sounds, no audio banks, no packed archives, no extracted
definition files.

References are not copies
-------------------------
The definitions refer to resources by path so that the game resolves them from
the user's own legally installed copy at load time:

  @include "sound_590s.sui"          engine sound configuration
  @include "sound.sui"               transmission sound configuration
  icon: "engine_scania_dc16"         existing part icon
  icon: "transmission_scania_grs"    existing part icon

The file paths under src/def/vehicle/truck/scania.r_2016/ are likewise
addresses the game requires in order to attach a part to that vehicle. None of
the referenced data is reproduced here. Without an installed copy of the game
this repository is inert.

Numbers are derived, not transcribed
------------------------------------
The torque curve, the rev limits, the shift windows, the ten gear ratios, the
final drive, the converter ratio and the retarder staging are all computed from
the design targets stated in docs/tuning.md, which shows the formulas and the
resulting values.

The parts are fictional
-----------------------
No manufacturer builds a 5000 hp truck engine. These parts are invented for a
game and are not representations, claims or specifications of any real product.
Part names are deliberately generic and marked "unofficial" for that reason.

